OL,3,GNEWSAFears for future of schools as
OL,4,Acity's pupil numbers set to drop by 17%
OL,5,
OL,6,FPupil numbers in Swansea are forecast
OL,7,Fto fall by more than 5,000 in six
OL,8,Fyears, challenging the long-term
OL,9,Fviability of some schools.
OL,11,FEducation officers have modelled the
OL,12,Fwider declining birth rate with
OL,13,Fspecific data for the city and estimate
OL,14,Fthere will be 26,678 primary and
OL,15,Fsecondary pupils in 2032 compared to
OL,16,F32,028 now ` a drop of 5,350 or 17%.
OL,18,FRobert Smith, Swansea council's cabinet
OL,19,Fmember for education and learning, said
OL,20,Fforecasting wasn't an exact science,
OL,21,Fbut that the figures "are as robust as
OL,22,Fthey can be".
OL,23,APub: 03-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
